module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.store_refusal_reported_as_contention

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data store_refusal_reported_as_contention: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "store_refusal_reported_as_contention" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a conditional-write realization reports every unsuccessful write as a lost precondition, without observing that a competing publication actually defeated the expectation. HARM: permission, capacity, or IO refusal becomes ordinary contention; the caller re-evaluates and retries against a phantom winner while the operational deficit disappears from its own refusal channel. This is the DESIGN section 5 refusal-as-contention widen, not a missing shared outcome.",

    "SPECIMEN, REPAIRED (silent-stag-307): cas_commit_at previously mapped every unsuccessful WriteOwnerOnly to CasPreconditionFailed via cas_probe_as_readable, including ProbedBeyondBound-as-absent. Publication now folds Filesystem.WriteCreateNew through filesystem_create_new. CasPreconditionFailed is emitted only for FilesystemCreateTargetOccupied together with a readable winner. Permission, other, unrecognized kinds, and occupied-with-no-readable-winner are CasStoreRefused. No error string is parsed. Observe uses cas_probe_as_observation, which preserves unreadability.",

    "EXECUTED, in CI run 34797864081 (hermetic, no real filesystem): test.claim.durable_cas_file_store_witness a_permission_refused_create_is_store_refused_not_contention, occupied_create_with_no_readable_winner_is_store_refused_not_contention, occupied_create_with_a_readable_winner_is_precondition_failed, and classifying_every_failed_publication_as_contention_turns_the_store_refusal_control_red (production versus cas_outcome_from_create_widening_every_failure_to_contention). Those four mock the filesystem; they do not prove fold plus real store.",

    "EXECUTED on BuildBuddy amd64: cargo test --release -p v1-compiler --lib write_file_create_new (11 tests), covering partial publication and direct_final_path_open_then_write_leaves_a_target_when_the_write_fails at the filesystem layer. That suite does not classify CasStoreRefused versus CasPreconditionFailed.",

    "NOT YET EXECUTED, receipt owed: the four test.claim.durable_cas_file_store_wet_witness identities (commit_then_independent_read_back_agrees_by_real_execution, a_second_eligible_writer_loses_to_the_observed_winner_by_real_execution, an_advance_after_commit_lands_generation_two_by_real_execution, a_non_contention_store_refusal_is_not_precondition_failed_by_real_execution). They are the only cells that run file_compare_and_set against a real filesystem. They are enrolled on the local-repo wet lane and route-gapped out of the hermetic floor (v2.workflow.floor_route_gap floor_route_gap_expectation_chunk_11), so floor green is silent about them by construction. The composed path -- fold plus real store -- therefore has no receipt this row may cite.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT BY EXECUTION: mechanically preventable at the hermetic classification fold and at the filesystem publication layer, at the grain of the two EXECUTED receipts above and no higher. Composition is not on that rung.",

    "CEILING: mechanically preventable at the external store boundary; the internal occupied-versus-refused partition is construction in cas_outcome_from_create. NEXT TRIGGER for composition: an executed receipt of the four wet identities on the local-repo wet lane. Remaining durability ceiling (crash-durable directory metadata) is a different class.",

    "FABRIC CONSUMER: gunbc.fabric_control_plane reserve_selected_cell maps CasPreconditionFailed to ReservationLost and CasStoreRefused to StoreUnavailable. Before this repair an unwritable store reported ReservationLost. After it, operational faults are StoreUnavailable. A genuine occupied slot is still ReservationLost. That is the observable change, and it is the defect closing rather than a silent shift of a correct race.",

    "CONSUMPTION: the derived gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.roster recurring_failure_mode_roster includes this per-class declaration.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.durable_cas_file_store", decl_name: "cas_outcome_from_create"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.durable_cas_file_store", decl_name: "cas_outcome_from_create_widening_every_failure_to_contention"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.durable_cas_file_store_witness", decl_name: "a_permission_refused_create_is_store_refused_not_contention"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.durable_cas_file_store_witness", decl_name: "classifying_every_failed_publication_as_contention_turns_the_store_refusal_control_red"),
  ],
}
